--- body ---

## Context

`Declaration.unsupported` was a set of verb names. A verb in it is absent, and
that is all the artifact could say. Two adapters reached the same objection
independently on 2026-09-02, each about a different verb, and each declined to
change the ratified contract on its own:

- the second adapter, on `pause` and `resume`: in its target's default
  configuration there is no unattended indexing at all, so there is no
  background work to pause. That is the architectural *opposite* of a target
  which has background work and exposes no control over it — and `unsupported`
  put both in the same cell. Its module docstring named the fix: mirror
  `not_derived_state`'s `(value, why)` shape.
- the first adapter, on `resume`: nothing maps onto it, because the only action
  that would continue an interrupted build is also the full rebuild and the
  repair. Mapping it would smuggle a destructive rebuild into the one verb the
  ruling says never rebuilds. That is a reason a reader needs, and it was
  reachable only by opening the adapter's source.

The two absences read identically in `checks.json`. One is a product gap; the
other is an architecture. Reading the second as the first is how a harness
invents a defect it then reports.

## Relevant files

- `bench/acceptance/interface.py` — `Declaration.unsupported`, its
  `__post_init__` validation, `as_json`, and `not_offered`.
- `bench/acceptance/adapters/zoteus.py` — `UNSUPPORTED`, whose docstring already
  argues both reasons at length.
- `bench/acceptance/adapters/zotero_mcp.py` — finding 4 of its module docstring
  is this ticket, written before the ticket existed.
- `bench/acceptance/adapters/stubs.py` — `stub-verbless`.

## Actions

1. `unsupported` becomes a mapping from verb to the reason it is absent,
   normalised to an immutable mapping at construction. `offers()` is unchanged.
2. A blank or whitespace-only reason is refused at construction. This is the
   whole of the change: a reason field adapters may leave empty is the same
   undifferentiated cell with a longer type.
3. The reason lands in the artifact twice — in the declaration, beside the
   sorted verb list that readers already parse, and on every `not-offered`
   verdict as `why_absent`, distinct from the harness's own `why`.
4. Every adapter fills it, in one line each, pointing at the docstring that
   argues it.

## Test

Red first, and against the unfixed tree rather than by argument. The three
blank-reason cases, the artifact-propagation case and the `not-offered`
verdict case must all fail at the baseline commit; the two that check
pre-existing behaviour — `offers()` still works, an unknown verb is still
refused — must pass there, or the test file is measuring something other than
this change.

## Verification

- [x] the new tests run red against `origin/main` at `ceadf71`: 5 failed,
      2 passed, the two passing ones being the pre-existing guards
- [x] `make check` green on the branch
- [x] no adapter declares an absent verb without a reason

## Invariants

- `offers()`, `VERBS`, `STATES` and the four verdicts are untouched. This
  widens one field of the declaration and nothing else.
- `unsupported_verbs` stays in the artifact as a sorted list, so a reader or a
  tool that already parses it is not broken by the addition beside it.

## Exit criteria
- [x] an absent verb carries its reason, and a blank one is refused
- [x] the reason reaches both the declaration and every `not-offered` verdict
- [x] every adapter's absent verbs carry theirs
- [x] the refusal was seen red against the unfixed tree before it was seen green
